# Decadic change log (human-readable; maintained per house RULE #2)

## 2026-06-17 — Self-model program Phase 0: integration-measurement scaffold

Goal (user request): implement the "Self-model feedback loop" plan, Phase 0 first — build the
falsification/integration-measurement track *before* any feedback pathway so every later phase
must prove it raises integration rather than relabel outputs.

New `decadic/metrics/` package (RULE #1, FORBIDDEN #3 — new module, ~210 lines):
- `integration.py`: a perturbational-complexity proxy (PCI / Φ-style). Drives a
  `NeuralCognitiveStack` with a fixed synthetic percept under `eval()`/`no_grad`, injects a
  single bounded pulse into `z0` at one cycle, and scores how widely/durably the pulse spreads
  across the per-stage 32-bin activation profiles vs an unperturbed baseline via the Lempel-Ziv
  (Kaspar-Schuster, 1976) complexity of the binarized deviation matrix. Returns `pci`, raw `lz`,
  `active_fraction`, `persistence`, `stage_spread`, and whether the self-feedback spine was
  driven. Probe resets the transient recurrent buffers on exit (no clobber of a live stack).
  `SELF_STATE_KEYS`/`self_state_vector()` define the canonical A‖C‖E vector the Phase-1 spine
  will feed back, so probe + live pipeline agree on "the self-report".
- `__init__.py`: re-exports the public surface.

New `tests/test_signatures.py` (Section-7 P1–P5 assays, capability-gated): Phase-0 instrument
tests run now (LZ properties, well-formed/bounded PCI, determinism, recurrent no-clobber); the
P1–P5 assays `skip` until their phase adds the faculty/flag, then auto-activate — keeps the suite
green at every step. 4 passed, 5 skipped.

Docs: added a "Self-model program" section to `docs/logical_layer_conformance.md` (the missing
edge, the falsification guard, and the phase→flag→signature table). No production cycle code
touched — Phase 0 is measurement only. Backups of all files Phase 1+ will touch saved to
`.\backups\*.20260617_113342.bak` (RULE #3).

