## 2026-06-17 — Long-horizon credit assignment, goal lifecycle, successor-value learning (+ anti-camping)

Goal: move the agent from "act until a drive is accidentally relieved" to "see a resource,
value it, walk to it, and learn the path that worked." True to the experiment: every new
component starts NAIVE (zero/identity init, ramped influence) and learns only from the
agent's own lived experience and its single innate drive (homeostatic reservoirs). Files
backed up to `.\backups\distal_credit_20260617_100700\` first (RULE #3).

Phase 0 — Scaffolding/config/safety. APIs confirmed against existing usage (RULE #6):
MuJoCo `model.body_pos[bid][i]` mutation is already exercised by `HumanoidSim.give_near`
(L1384-1410); PyTorch TD(lambda)/successor-features are classic and need no new dependency.
Added config blocks to `decadic/config.py` (env-var pattern, all live-overridable):
- Per-life resource randomization: `randomize_resources_enabled` (default ON),
  `resource_placement_mode` (arena|zone), `resource_min_dist`, `resource_fence_margin`.
- Goal lifecycle: `goal_onset_deficit`, `goal_satisfy_level`, `goal_abandon_cycles`,
  `goal_max_cycles`.
- Distal credit + successor features: `sf_enabled`, `sf_gamma`, `sf_lambda`,
  `sf_loss_weight`, `sf_value_weight`, `sf_value_ramp_cycles`, `sf_value_weight_for_cycle`
  (linear 0->max ramp so a fresh agent is byte-identical to today until experience grows it).
- HER: `her_enabled`, `her_relabel_k`. Imagination (default OFF): `imagination_enabled`,
  `imagination_horizon`, `imagination_weight`.
No change to `decadic/nn/config.py`: the SF head reuses `motor_hidden` and outputs the
existing `INTERO_PRED_DIM` (3) feature dim, so the preset table / checkpoint shape is
untouched.

Phase 1 — Per-life random resource placement (anti-camping).
- NEW `decadic/embodiment/resource_placement.py` (pure, MuJoCo-free): `scatter_positions`
  picks fresh XY for each consumable, uniform-by-area in the arena disc (kept >= min_dist
  from origin, inside the fence margin) or within random habitat zones. Unit-tested.
- `scripts/mujoco_decadic_adapter.py`: new `HumanoidSim._randomize_resources(seed)` writes
  `model.body_pos` for every static (non-gift) food/water prop, un-hides + cancels pending
  respawns, clears `eaten`, `mj_forward`s, and stores `_resource_seed`. Gift bodies (free-
  joint parent provisions) are intentionally left to the delivery FSM. Called once at body
  spawn (after `recenter()` in `__init__`) and via a new `randomize_resources[:seed]` WS
  body command. Imports the four resource config accessors + `active_habitats`.
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: `revive()` now queues `recenter` + `randomize_resources:<seed>`
  on each new life (mind weights/memory untouched; only body pose + world layout reset) and
  records the seed in `metrics["resource_seed"]` (new metric, default -1). Added
  `randomize_resources_enabled` import + `import random`.
Smoke test confirmed deterministic scatter, min-dist invariant, and config wiring.

Phase 2 — Goal lifecycle state + telemetry.
- NEW `decadic/state/goal_lifecycle.py` (pure): `GoalState.update(reservoirs, cycle, alive)`
  latches the dominant normalized deficit as the active goal once it crosses
  `onset_deficit`, holds it, and emits `GoalEvent`s on close: achieved (reservoir back
  >= satisfy_level), abandoned (a different need dominates for abandon_cycles), truncated
  (max_cycles), or died. `dwell()` reports cycles-open; `episodes`/`last_outcome` track
  history. The closed [onset->close] window is the episode the return learner trains on.
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: owns one `GoalState` (built in `__init__` from the goal
  config), new `_reservoirs_norm()` + `_advance_goal(transition)` helper called each cycle
  in `_cycle_loop` (after the replay push). Surfaces `goal`, `goal_status`, `goal_dwell`,
  `goal_episodes`, `goal_last_outcome` in metrics (added to `_initial_metrics`). Added the
  four goal config imports + `GoalState`.
Smoke test confirmed latch/achieve/abandon+reopen/death transitions.

Phase 3 — Episodic replay timeline (distal credit assignment).
- `decadic/consolidation/replay_buffer.py`: extended `Transition` with additive,
  inert-by-default fields: `feat` (per-step phi = reservoir change), `reward` (innate-
  weighted phi = drive reduction), `episode_id`/`step_idx`/`goal_id`, and `ret`/`sf_target`
  (lambda-return scalar + discounted-future-feature vector, filled on episode close;
  `ret=None` until then gates the SF loss).
- NEW `decadic/consolidation/returns.py` (pure): forward-view `lambda_returns` (scalar) and
  `lambda_returns_vec` (vector successor-feature targets), terminal bootstrap 0, optional
  value bootstrap for TD(lambda). Unit-tested (MC limit, lam<1 smear, TD(0)).
- NEW `decadic/consolidation/episodes.py`: `EpisodeAccumulator` collects ordered transitions
  per open goal, stamps episode/step/goal ids, and on close computes returns and writes
  `ret`/`sf_target` back IN PLACE (the same refs already in the replay buffer -> no second
  push, existing one-step consolidation data flow untouched). Bounded retained refs.
- `decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py`: transition payload now carries `feat` (phi) + `reward`
  computed from the realized reservoir transition with the innate preference weights.
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: owns one `EpisodeAccumulator` (built in `__init__`, rebuilt on
  `reset()`, dangling episode dropped on `revive()`); `_cycle_loop` builds the `Transition`,
  pushes it, then routes it + the goal events through `_accumulate_episode` (add-then-apply
  so an achieving step lands in the episode it completes); `die()` closes the open episode as
  "died". New telemetry `episodes_closed`/`episode_last_len`/`episode_last_return`. A no-op
  `_maybe_hindsight_relabel` hook is reserved for Phase 5.
Smoke test confirmed distal reward propagation, in-place annotation, and stats.

Phase 4 — Successor-features head + value + policy shaping (Layer-2).
- NEW `decadic/nn/successor_features.py`: `SuccessorFeaturesHead.predict(state, u, detach_params)`
  -- twin of the proprio/intero forward heads (two linears + functional detach trick); OUTPUT
  layer zero-initialized so psi == 0 (and value == 0) at birth.
- `decadic/nn/neural_stack.py`: thin wiring only -- instantiate `self.sf_head` next to the
  forward heads (`has_successor_model=True`) and a delegating `successor_predict(...)`. The SF
  head is NEVER called from `forward()`, so the stack's forward output is byte-identical.
- `decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py`: added the value-shaping term inside the drive block --
  `v = (innate_deficit_gated_w * psi(z5, motor_u, detach_params=True)).sum()`, `loss -= vw*v`
  with `vw = sf_value_weight_for_cycle(cycle)` ramping 0->max. SF weights detached
  (anti-hallucination); finiteness-guarded. New diagnostics `sf_value` + `sf_value_weight`.
- `decadic/consolidation/consolidator.py`: `replay_batch_loss` now adds the SF TD(lambda)
  regression `MSE(psi(prev_state, prev_motor), sf_target)` for return-annotated transitions
  (`sf_target` filled on episode close). SF is therefore trained off the critical path and
  flows to the live stack via the existing Polyak soft-sync (sf_head is in the state_dict).
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: copies `sf_value`/`sf_value_weight` from diagnostics into
  metrics (defaults added to `_initial_metrics`).
Smoke test confirmed psi zero-init parity, learnability, and state_dict round-trip.

Phase 5 — Hindsight relabeling (HER).
- `decadic/consolidation/episodes.py`: `achieved_feature(steps)` = net per-channel phi over the
  episode; `build_hindsight_copies(steps, achieved, gamma, lam, k)` recomputes SF/return targets
  with the achieved terminal feature as the success bootstrap and emits `k` relabeled COPIES
  (shared detached tensor refs; only credit fields + goal tag differ).
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: `_maybe_hindsight_relabel` (the Phase-3 hook) now fires on a
  non-achieved close when the trajectory still accrued relief in some channel (e.g. latched on
  thirst but actually ate), pushing the relabeled copies into the salience buffer so the SF head
  trains more on the off-goal relief it really found. Gated by `her_enabled`/`her_relabel_k`; new
  metrics `her_relabels`/`her_last`. Note: because the SF target is goal-INDEPENDENT and
  physically real, HER here densifies real near-miss relief rather than fabricating innate reward.
Smoke test confirmed achieved-feature, k copies, ref-sharing, and bootstrap-shifted targets.

Phase 6 — Model-based imagined replay (Dreamer-lite, gated, default OFF).
- NEW `decadic/consolidation/imagination.py`: `imagined_sf_loss(stack, batch, gamma, horizon,
  device)` rolls the interoceptive forward model forward (start state+action held) under
  no_grad to build an imagined discounted successor-feature target, and regresses the trainable
  SF head toward it. Bounded horizon; honest note that no latent-dynamics model exists so only
  the interoceptive channel is imagined.
- `decadic/consolidation/consolidator.py`: `consolidate_once` adds the trust-weighted imagined
  SF loss (gated by `sf_enabled` AND `imagination_enabled`, default off) OUTSIDE the shared
  `replay_loss` so the loss-landscape probe still scores the pure lived objective. New
  `last_imagined_loss` telemetry.
Smoke test confirmed finite imagined loss, backprop into the SF head, and no-op on non-drive.

