## 2026-06-16 — Live agent performance: GPU + bf16 HF encoders

Goal: lift the running agent from ~1 Hz toward a human-realistic 10–20 Hz WITHOUT
changing the science — keep `full` + HF perception on, keep wall-clock metabolic /
consolidation constants, keep the trainable stack fp32. Every change is device-gated
so the `cpu`/`zeros`/`fp32`-pinned test suite (`tests/conftest.py`) stays
byte-identical (465 passed, 7 skipped, unchanged).

Root cause: a ~25M-param stack + CLIP ViT-B/32 + Whisper-small were training every
cycle, and `torch` historically resolved to a CPU-only wheel — CPU was the whole
bottleneck (the cycle profiler below shows fwd+bwd dominates). The hot path was
already device-aware, so this was "turn the GPU on + trim CPU work," not a rewrite.
(NOTE: this environment already has `torch 2.11.0+cu128` with CUDA available, so the
big lever was just pinning the device + the bf16/dedup trims.)

Phase 0 — Measure first (RULE #6): reused the pipeline's existing per-section timers
(`neural_forward_ms`, `neural_backward_ms`, `encode_phase_ms`, `enc_ms`, `mem_ms`,
`ms10`) instead of instrumenting the hot path. Surfaced `encoders_ms` /
`memory_recall_ms` / `stage10_ms` in the diagnostics dict and added a
`DECADIC_CYCLE_PROFILE=1` cycle log of the split (`runtime._cycle_loop`). Off by
default, near-zero cost.

Phase 1 — GPU enablement: pinned `DECADIC_DEVICE=cuda` in `scripts/launch_decadic.ps1`
(auto-falls-back to CPU if CUDA absent); added a startup log in `bundle.try_build`
(`neural compute device=… gpu=… vram_free_gb=… bf16=…`). The consolidation clone +
landscape probe inherit `bundle.device` for free.

Phase 2 — bf16 frozen encoders (device-gated): `config.encoder_autocast_dtype()`
(`DECADIC_ENCODER_PRECISION=auto|bf16|fp16|fp32`, default `auto`). In
`frozen_encoders.py` the CLIP/Whisper forwards autocast to bf16 on a bf16-capable
CUDA device and are cast back to fp32 before the fusion `cat`; CPU stays fp32. The
trainable proprio MLP + stack are never autocast.

Phase 3 — De-dup CLIP: cache the spatial patch-token grid keyed on `obs["timestamp"]`
(mirrors the pooled cache), so repeated cycles consuming one frame skip the CLIP
vision_model forward (cached `None` honored for image-less frames).

Phase 4 — Episodic write off the lock (flagged OFF): new
`decadic/memory/write_behind.py` `WriteBehindEpisodicStore` (subclass of
`EpisodicStore`) defers the per-cycle SQLite append to a daemon worker; reads are
inherited, no write is lost (sync fallback on a full queue), `clear`/`backup`/
`restore` flush first. Gated by `DECADIC_EPISODIC_ASYNC` (default OFF), pinned OFF in
conftest, worker drained in `runtime.stop()`.

New files:
- `decadic/memory/write_behind.py` — write-behind episodic store (<110 lines).
- `tests/test_encoder_precision.py` — CPU fp32 parity (unconditional) + CUDA-gated
  bf16 finite/fp32/shape smoke + CLIP patch-token cache hit/recompute.
- `tests/test_write_behind.py` — persistence-after-flush, search parity, clear-flush,
  backpressure-never-drops (all CPU-only).

Edits (originals backed up to `.\backups\*.20260616_232629.bak`):
- `decadic/config.py` — `cycle_profile_enabled()`, `encoder_autocast_dtype()`,
  `episodic_async_enabled()`.
- `decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py` — surface `encoders_ms`/`memory_recall_ms`/
  `stage10_ms` in diagnostics.
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py` — `cycle_profile` log; conditional write-behind store;
  worker close in `stop()`.
- `decadic/nn/bundle.py` — CUDA/CPU startup device + VRAM + bf16 log.
- `decadic/nn/frozen_encoders.py` — `_encoder_autocast()`, bf16-then-fp32 around the
  three frozen forwards, patch-token cache (`_compute_patch_tokens` split out).
- `scripts/launch_decadic.ps1` — pin `DECADIC_DEVICE=cuda`.
- `tests/conftest.py` — pin `DECADIC_ENCODER_PRECISION=fp32`, `DECADIC_EPISODIC_ASYNC=0`,
  `DECADIC_CYCLE_PROFILE=0`.
- `README.md` — new "Performance / GPU" section + env rows + cognition-vs-wallclock
  caveat.

Verification: `tests/test_encoder_precision.py` + `tests/test_write_behind.py` → 8
passed (bf16 + patch-cache actually ran on the RTX 3080); full suite 465 passed,
7 skipped (no regressions). GPU smoke: `device=cuda gpu=NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080
vram_free_gb=8.9 bf16=True`; bf16 encoder fused output dtype=float32 shape (1,1344)
finite; patch tokens float32 (1,49,768).

## 2026-06-16 — Stance & motion ROM braces (selectable braced postures)

Goal: let the operator put the agent in postures to learn — stand & balance,
all-fours, kneel (twist left/right), plus motions (crawl, rise) — by extending the
joint-brace system with a selectable stance library. A stance re-poses the body
(root height/orientation + per-joint reference) and re-welds the braces toward
that pose; the existing ROM curriculum then loosens each joint as prediction error
falls. A motion is a time-varying reference the stiff braces track, so travel comes
from REAL contact with the floor. The root is never forced — the no-glide invariant
holds in every stance (`xfrc_applied[torso]` stays zero, asserted in tests).

New file:
- `decadic/embodiment/stances.py` — single source of truth (pure data + resolvers,
  no MuJoCo). `Stance` dataclass (label, joints deg, root_z, root_quat, fall_z, and
  optional motion keyframes/period/loop). `STANCES` registry: stand, all_fours,
  kneel_left, kneel_right (static) + crawl, sit_to_stand (motion). `resolve()` maps
  deg->rad and clamps ONLY authored joints (unspecified hinges keep qpos0 verbatim,
  so stand == the validated zero pose); `motion_ref()` interpolates/wraps keyframes;
  `catalog()` feeds the UI. <~330 lines.

Edits (surgical; originals backed up to `.\backups\stance_20260616_220338\`):
- `scripts/mujoco_decadic_adapter.py`: capture `hinge_names` + per-hinge ranges;
  active-stance state (`_stance_name/_stance_phase/_stance_root_z/_stance_root_quat/
  _stance_fall_z`); `_q_ref` now resolved from the active stance; `set_stance(name)`
  (re-pose via stance-aware `recenter()` + `reset_braces()`); `_advance_motion()` in
  `step()` retargets `_q_ref`+`qpos_spring` from the motion phase before the brace
  tick; `recenter()` uses the stance root pose (still preserves earned ROM); `stance`
  /`stance_phase` on `BodySnapshot` + obs JSON; per-stance `fall_height` into
  `body_events`; WS `set_stance:NAME` dispatch.
- `decadic/api/app.py`: `GET /body/stances` (catalog) + `POST /agent/{id}/body/
  stance?name=...` (queues `set_stance:NAME`).
- `decadic/agents/runtime.py`: `stance`/`stance_phase` in `_initial_metrics` and
  mirrored in `_capture_locomotion_telemetry` (dashboard-only; inert to cognition).
- `dashboard/src/api.ts`: `stance`/`stance_phase` on `Metrics`, `STANCES` constant,
  `setStance()`. `dashboard/src/components/MotorPanel.tsx`: a "Stance" selector
  button group (active highlighted) + a phase readout for motion stances.
- `scripts/_gen_stand_pose.py`: `settle_stance()` settle-checks each stance under
  full braces (finite / support loads / drift / root_z). `scripts/_probe_pose.py`:
  pose-authoring probe (per-geom world-z + COM at spawn) used to tune the poses.

Pose tuning notes (validated stable, drift over a 6 s braced settle):
- stand 0.007, all_fours 0.137 (hands+feet bear), kneel_left/right ~0.09
  (knees-down quadruped, torso twisted L/R), crawl/sit_to_stand start 0.137.
- A free-root statue held only by position-braces obeys COM-over-support: an upright
  single-knee kneel and a deep bipedal squat are NOT statically holdable on this
  humanoid (joint ranges shoot the feet ahead of the COM and it tips), so the kneels
  are realized as a stable knees-down quadruped distinguished by torso twist, and
  `sit_to_stand` ("Rise up") is a stable push-up from all-fours (leg/elbow extension)
  rather than a full bipedal stand. Full sit-to-stand needs dynamic balance — noted
  as future work (alongside the separately-scoped balance-gated ROM curriculum).

Verification: full `pytest` 457 passed, 7 skipped; 7 new stance tests (resolve
clamp/defaults, catalog/motion flags, motion interp+wrap, set_stance re-pose/re-weld,
no external wrench per stance, motion advances q_ref, posture-aware fall floor);
dashboard `npm run build` (tsc+vite) OK; TestClient `GET /body/stances` returns the
6-stance catalog.

## 2026-06-16 — Live loss-landscape visualization (filter-normalized brain surface)

Goal: render the loss surface from the reference image *live*, for the agent's actual
brain — `L(a,b) = loss(theta* + a·d1 + b·d2)` over a 2D grid of filter-normalized
weight-space directions, drawn as a 3D mesh in the dashboard with the current weights
theta* marked at the center. Reuses the dual-network consolidation machinery so the
plotted surface is the agent's TRUE training objective (predictive coding + proprioceptive
+ interoceptive forward models), not a proxy. Default OFF: visualization-only, expensive,
and never touches the live weights — enabling it is byte-identical to baseline cognition.

Problem / why:
- The user asked for a live version of the loss-landscape plot showing the agent's brain.
- A meaningful surface needs (a) the real objective, (b) filter normalization (Li et al.,
  2018) so the geometry is not a weight-scale artifact, (c) a throwaway clone so the live
  agent is never perturbed, and (d) off-critical-path background compute + caching.

Design:
- Shared objective (DRY): extracted module-level `replay_batch_loss(stack, batch, device)`
  in consolidator.py; `ConsolidationManager.replay_loss` now delegates to it, so the probe
  and the consolidator score the IDENTICAL loss. Consolidation tests guard parity.
- Filter-normalized directions: two seeded Gaussian directions over params with dim>=2
  (the network's "filters"), each filter rescaled to its weight filter's norm; 1-D params
  (biases/norm gains) held fixed. Seeded/persisted so the bowl is comparable frame-to-frame.
- Recurrent state zeroed before every grid-point eval, so the surface is a pure function of
  (weights, batch, directions) — no evaluation-order contamination from the GRU/LSTM buffers.

New files:
- decadic/consolidation/landscape.py (NEW, ~190 lines): LossLandscapeProbe — own clone,
  filter_normalized_directions, no-grad grid `compute()` returning the JSON surface dict.
- dashboard/src/components/LandscapePanel.tsx (NEW): react-three-fiber surface mesh built
  from z[][], RdYlBu height/color map, theta* marker sphere, warming-up empty state; reuses
  BrainMapPanel's Canvas/OrbitControls conventions. Polls every 4 s.
- tests/test_landscape.py (NEW, 11 tests): direction norms + 1-D skip, seed determinism,
  grid shape + finiteness, center_loss == consolidator held_out_loss, no live-weight
  mutation, empty-batch None, grid clamp, runtime parity-when-off, API 404/202/200.

Wiring (thin hooks; every edited file backed up to .\backups\ first per RULE #3):
- decadic/config.py: DEFAULT_LANDSCAPE_* + accessors landscape_enabled() (default 0),
  landscape_grid()/span()/batch()/interval_s()/seed().
- decadic/agents/runtime.py: _landscape_task/_landscape_probe/_last_landscape; start
  _landscape_runner in ensure_cycle_worker when (flag AND neural AND replay_buffer); the
  runner samples the buffer, runs probe.compute via asyncio.to_thread on a cadence, caches
  the surface, logs `landscape_compute` (cycle/grid/batch/center/min/max/wall_ms); cancel in
  stop(); clear in reset(); brain_landscape() accessor.
- decadic/api/app.py: GET /agent/{id}/brain/landscape (404 unknown / 202 warming up / 200).
- dashboard/src/api.ts: BrainLandscape type + fetchBrainLandscape().
- dashboard/src/App.tsx: "Loss Landscape" tab + LandscapePanel render.
- tests/conftest.py: pin DECADIC_LANDSCAPE_ENABLED=0 in _baseline_faculties for parity.

Docs: README.md gains a "Loss Landscape (live)" subsection + the DECADIC_LANDSCAPE_* env
var rows. Plan file: .cursor/plans (untouched per instruction).

Verification:
- tests/test_landscape.py: 11 passed. tests/test_consolidation.py: 13 passed (parity held
  after the replay_batch_loss extraction). dashboard `tsc --noEmit`: clean.
- Full suite: 450 passed, 7 skipped (the 11 new landscape tests; no regressions).

## 2026-06-16 — Persistent long-term knowledge graph (hippocampal index)

Goal: add the missing long-term half of the memory architecture. Working memory
stays bounded (K=7 slots / capacity 12 — the "what's present now" buffer), but
there was no growing relational long-term memory: the only graph was rebuilt
from scratch every observation and thrown away, capped at the slot bottleneck.
This adds a persistent, unbounded relational knowledge graph (the hippocampal
index) that working memory consolidates into and reinstates from, plus a
dedicated dashboard panel to watch it grow. All paths ship ON by default.

Changes:
- decadic/memory/semantic_graph.py (NEW, 382 lines): LongTermGraph — SQLite-backed
  (in-memory fallback), thread-safe, UNBOUNDED node/edge store. match() does
  cosine re-identification by appearance; upsert_node() coins stable ent-NNNNN
  ids or EMA-updates a matched node; bump_edge() accumulates co-occurrence edges;
  consolidate(slots) commits stable slots + links co-present ones; snapshot(limit)
  is a windowed read-out carrying total_nodes/total_edges; backup_to/restore_from
  mirror the episodic-store SQLite backup pattern.
- decadic/memory/__init__.py: export LongTermGraph.
- decadic/config.py: ltm_graph_enabled() (env DECADIC_LTM_GRAPH) DEFAULTS TRUE,
  plus ltm_match_threshold/ltm_consolidate_min_seen/ltm_snapshot_limit. (Contrast:
  consolidation_enabled stays the existing behavior; the flag is only a parity
  escape hatch.)
- decadic/cycle/types.py: CycleContext gains ltm_graph (default None -> parity).
- decadic/agents/registry.py + runtime.py: construct per-agent
  agent_<id>_graph.sqlite; hold it on AgentRuntime (None only when disabled);
  inject into every CycleContext; clear() on reset; backup_graph_to/restore_graph_from;
  merge ltm_graph.snapshot(limit) into the perceptual payload (snapshot_state).
- decadic/cycle/stages/stage_10.py: consolidation write (WM -> LTM) each cycle,
  gated on discovered mode + a stability criterion (seen_count >= min_seen).
- decadic/state/working_memory.py: integrate_discovered gains an optional
  reidentify hook (LTM -> WM read); a coin-path hit rebinds to the persistent
  ent-NNNNN id so the "now" graph and the long-term graph share identities.
  reidentify=None -> byte-identical to before (oracle / no-LTM parity).
- decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py: pass ctx.ltm_graph.match as reidentify when
  the graph is present.
- decadic/api/saved_agents/store.py + routes.py: graph.sqlite save artifact
  (GRAPH_NAME, SavePaths.graph, SCHEMA_VERSION 1 -> 2), copied on save/restore so
  saved agents carry their accumulated long-term graph. Missing file -> no-op.
- dashboard/src/api.ts: LtmNode/LtmEdge/LtmGraphSnapshot types; perceptual.ltm_graph.
- dashboard/src/components/LongTermMemoryPanel.tsx (NEW, 194 lines): force-directed
  relational view; node color = a deterministic hue of the appearance embedding
  (NO semantic labels), size = times seen, rim = consolidated affect; headline
  total_nodes/total_edges counters so growth is observable.
- dashboard/src/App.tsx + style.css: mount the panel next to the bounded "now"
  graph on the Self-Indexed Graph tab; .ltm-* styles.
- tests/test_semantic_graph.py (NEW): store (upsert/match/growth/edges/
  consolidate/persistence/clear) + wiring (reinstatement rebinds to the long-term
  id; no-reidentify parity; LTM grows while WM stays bounded; default-on).

House rules: backups of every edited file in .\backups\ (suffix .20260616_170045.bak);
ai.md added for decadic/memory and dashboard/src/components. New files are all
< 500 lines. Pre-existing oversized files (runtime.py, config.py, api.ts,
working_memory.py) were touched minimally and are flagged as separate refactors.

Verification: full pytest 439 passed, 7 skipped; dashboard `npm run build`
(tsc + vite) OK; live smoke (AgentRuntime) confirms the graph is constructed by
default and rides in the API payload (perceptual.ltm_graph, totals 0/0 fresh).

