## 2026-06-16 — Dual-network memory consolidation (Option B)

Plan: .cursor/plans/curiosity_consolidation_babylon_cleanup_9867a073.plan.md
(Phase 3 of 3 — final phase.)

Problem: the consolidation subsystem was a no-op stub heartbeat. Salient experience
was stored in episodic memory but never *re-learned* — there was no replay-based
long-term learning, no forgetting of stale low-salience experience, and the brief's
Phase 3 (dual-network setup with periodic weight sync) was unimplemented.

Design: Option B (dual-network). A second cloned cognitive stack replays
salience-prioritized transitions on its OWN optimizer, recomputing the same
self-supervised PC / forward-model / interoceptive losses the live cycle uses, then
periodically Polyak soft-syncs its weights back into the live stack under the agent
lock. Replay runs in a thread executor (asyncio.to_thread) so the cognitive cycle is
never blocked. OFF by default -> the runtime keeps the no-op stub heartbeat and live
weights stay byte-identical to baseline.

New files:
- decadic/consolidation/replay_buffer.py (~200 lines): Transition (detached CPU
  latents needed to recompute the cycle's losses + salience) and ReplayBuffer
  (fixed capacity, salience-prioritized sample() with replacement, lowest-salience
  eviction when full + a prune-floor = built-in forgetting, threading.Lock for the
  cross-thread push/sample race).
- decadic/consolidation/consolidator.py (~290 lines): ConsolidationManager clones the
  active NeuralCognitiveStack, owns an Adam optimizer, implements replay_loss /
  held_out_loss / consolidate_once (one gradient step) / soft_sync (Polyak, NaN-safe,
  zero-tau no-op) and an async run_loop of periodic replay+sync bursts.

Wiring (backups tag 20260616_102120 covers the doc sweep; code edits backed up under
earlier tags):
- decadic/config.py: DEFAULT_CONSOLIDATION_* + consolidation_enabled() (default off) /
  replay_buffer_size() / consolidation_replay_batch() / consolidation_steps_per_burst()
  / consolidation_sync_tau() / consolidation_sync_interval_s() /
  consolidation_prune_min_salience() (env DECADIC_CONSOLIDATION_* + DECADIC_REPLAY_BUFFER_SIZE).
- decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py: when consolidation_enabled(), package a detached
  CPU _transition payload (z0, ep, mem, prev_state, prev_motor, proprio target,
  prev/next intero, drive_on, salience) into the cycle return dict; zero-cost when off.
- decadic/agents/runtime.py: build self.replay_buffer iff enabled; per-cycle push of
  the _transition payload; _consolidation_runner routes to ConsolidationManager.run_loop
  when enabled (else the existing consolidation_stub_loop heartbeat); _on_consolidation_sync
  callback feeds replay_count / consolidator_loss / last_sync_cycle / replay_buffer_size
  into metrics (defaults added to _initial_metrics).

Tests: tests/test_consolidation.py (13 cases) -- ReplayBuffer (capacity, lowest-salience
eviction, prune floor, prioritized sampling favors high salience, stats), ConsolidationManager
(clone parity, a replay step reduces held-out loss, soft-sync moves live toward consolidator
without NaNs, zero-tau no-op), pipeline transition emission when on, and runtime buffer wiring
(present iff enabled). Assertions are directional/statistical given async timing.

Verification: python -m pytest -q => 390 passed, 7 skipped (377 prior + 13 new; baseline
unchanged -> parity confirmed with the flag off). Lints clean.

## 2026-06-16 — Need-gated curiosity drive (autonomous epistemic motivation)

Plan: .cursor/plans/curiosity_consolidation_babylon_cleanup_9867a073.plan.md
(Phase 2 of 3.)

Problem: cognition had no autonomous epistemic motivation. Exploration came only
from unmet homeostatic need (motor babble) -- a sated, safe agent had no reason
to investigate the world, and there was no "interest" signal in element B. The
user asked for curiosity to fire autonomously, as part of the cognition stage,
as need arises.

Design: curiosity = a *learning-progress* epistemic drive (reward the reduction
of forward-model prediction error, NOT raw surprise -> avoids the noisy-TV trap),
folded into the existing pain/pleasure -> element B path as a pleasure-side affect
and need-gated by survival urgency (suppressed under threat/deprivation, expressed
when safe and sated). Mirrors the innate homeostatic-drive pattern (phylogeny
fixes the substrate; "what is interesting" is learned) and Stage 4's risk-vs-
curiosity arbitration. OFF by default -> byte-identical baseline.

New file:
- decadic/state/curiosity.py (~230 lines, pure + one small stateful class):
  learning_progress() (relative fall of PE over a rolling window, clamped [0,1]),
  survival_urgency()/permission() (the need-gate), epistemic_opportunity()
  (progress + a small current-error floor so a flat-but-wrong state still probes),
  curiosity_signal() -> (pain=0, pleasure), and CuriosityState/compute_curiosity()
  returning the gated drive, pleasure, learning_progress, permission, and an
  investigate flag.

Thin hooks (backups tag 20260616_095936):
- decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py: import + a single guarded block before the
  babble gate that updates the bundle's ephemeral PE history (bundle._curiosity,
  never checkpointed) and computes the drive; its drive is ADDED to the
  motor_exploration_sigma `drive` arg (so satisfied curiosity lets babble relax);
  its pleasure is injected into B and floors pleasure_scalar (mirrors drive_pain
  on the pleasure axis); priority_label flips "explore" -> "investigate" when the
  epistemic value clears a small threshold and the agent is not avoiding.
  curiosity_drive/pleasure/learning_progress added to the diagnostics dict (None
  when off -> parity).
- decadic/config.py: DEFAULT_CURIOSITY_* + curiosity_enabled() (default off) /
  curiosity_gain() / curiosity_progress_window() / curiosity_safety_sharpness()
  (env DECADIC_CURIOSITY_*). [config.py is already >500 lines; refactor flagged
  for a future pass per PHILOSOPHY #1, additions kept to flat accessors.]
- decadic/agents/runtime.py: curiosity_drive/pleasure/learning_progress in
  _initial_metrics + copied from diagnostics in _apply_cycle_diagnostics
  (only when present -> off-parity), so they surface on GET /agent/{id}/metrics.

Tests: tests/test_curiosity.py (29 cases) -- learning-progress math (short/flat/
rising/falling/bounded/mastered), urgency+permission gate, opportunity+signal
(rises with progress, suppressed under pain/low-viability, gain scaling, no pain
side), stateful investigate decision, and end-to-end via run_neural_cycle
(parity when off; enters pleasure affect + telemetry; priority -> investigate;
suppressed under low viability).

Verification: python -m pytest -q => 377 passed, 7 skipped (348 baseline + 29
new; baseline unchanged -> parity confirmed with the flag off). Lints clean.

