## 2026-06-16 — Saved Agents library (durable save + load-from-UI)

Plan: .cursor/plans/saved_agents_library_09e29602.plan.md

Goal (user request): a place to SAVE agents that is separate from the checkpoint
system, with agents loadable back in via the UI. Decisions (confirmed): full
build (backend + dashboard), memory ALWAYS bundled, store at saved_agents/
(env-overridable via DECADIC_SAVED_DIR).

Why separate: backups/ checkpoints are ephemeral — keyed by the volatile agent
uuid and pruned to N-most-recent on death (AgentRuntime._prune_tombstones globs
backups/agent_*_brain.pt), and /restore only works for an id still live in the
process. The new library is keyed by a stable save_id folder, never auto-pruned,
and loads into a fresh agent (re-keyed onto a new uuid like the vast restore),
so saves survive restarts.

