## 2026-06-15 — Floor condim=6 (arrest rolling glide)

Follow-up to Contacts and No-Glide. The supine body still appeared to "slide on
glass": the cause was free ROLLING, not sliding. condim=3 contacts only model
sliding friction; torsional/rolling friction (the 2nd/3rd friction numbers)
require condim>=4/6. The body is mostly round capsules/spheres, so it rolled
freely on the floor at any sliding friction.

Change: assets/humanoid_body.xml floor geom condim 3 -> 6 (friction kept at
"1 .1 .1"). MuJoCo takes the MAX condim of the two contacting geoms, so every
body-vs-floor contact is now condim=6 and the rolling (0.1) + torsional (0.1)
coefficients finally apply. Backup: .\backups\humanoid_body.xml.20260615_102908.bak

Verification: headless supine body shoved at linear 2.0 m/s + angular 6.0 rad/s
decelerates to |w|~1.2 and vx~0.03 over 3 s (travel ~0.49 m) instead of rolling
freely. pytest (walking/motor/proprio) 52 passed; body geom condim==3 tests
unaffected (only the floor changed).

