## 2026-06-16 — Fix "vastai CLI not found" (bundle + PATH-independent detection)

Bug: the Deploy/GPU tab reported "The vastai CLI was not found on the server"
even though it should ship with the project. Root causes: (1) vastai was not a
dependency, so it was never installed; (2) detection used only
shutil.which("vastai"), which misses a venv/user-site install whose Scripts dir
is off PATH; (3) the invocation fallback used `python -m vastai`, but the package
has no __main__ so that never worked.

Why (7 levels): not found -> available() False -> only checked PATH -> the
console script (vastai.exe) installs to a user-site Scripts dir
(C:\Users\...\AppData\Roaming\Python\Python313\Scripts) that is not on PATH ->
pip put it there because the package was installed ad hoc, not as a project dep
-> it was never declared in pyproject -> the feature shipped assuming a manual
install. Fix all three.

Backups (pre-edit) in .\backups\ (timestamp 20260616_*):
- pyproject.toml.<ts>.bak, cli.py.<ts>.bak

Changes:
- pyproject.toml: add `vastai>=1.0` to runtime dependencies (bundled).
- decadic/api/vast/cli.py: resolve_vastai_bin() is now PATH-independent —
  override -> PATH -> console script in any interpreter-adjacent scripts dir
  (incl. the user-site one) -> run the entry point `vastai.cli.main:main` via the
  server's own interpreter (`python -c` shim) whenever the package is importable.
  available() returns True if vastai is on PATH OR importable OR a script is
  found. Dropped the broken `python -m vastai` fallback.
- deploy/vast/README.md: prereqs note vastai is bundled (no manual install /
  PATH edit) + a restart reminder for an already-running server.
- Installed vastai-1.0.13 into the server interpreter (C:\Python313, user site).

Verification: VastCli().available() -> True; resolve_vastai_bin() ->
