## 2026-06-16 — GPU model is now a live dropdown (pulled from Vast)

Feature: the Deploy/GPU "GPU model" field is a dropdown populated from Vast's
live marketplace instead of free-typing. Distinct rentable model names + an
availability count, e.g. "RTX 5090 (236)". An "Any GPU" option searches across
all models; a ↻ button refreshes the list.

Why deduped offers (not `metrics gpu`): `vastai metrics gpu` is a host command
requiring the machine_read permission group, which a normal renter key lacks
(verified live: 401). So the names are derived from a broad
`search offers rentable=true -n --limit N` and deduped on `gpu_name`. Vast
reports names with spaces ("RTX 5090") but query filters need underscores
("RTX_5090"), so the API returns both (value=underscored, name=spaced).

