## 2026-06-17 — Real cycle affect: replace the PE and reward stubs

Two live placeholders in the neural cognitive cycle were arbitrary scaffolding
that contaminated the affect channel; both are now grounded in the agent's own
dynamics (intrinsic only — no external/labeled reward, no clock):

- `stub_prediction_error_penalty` added a deterministic cycle-counter oscillation
  on top of the genuine surprise signal (the predictive-coding loss). It is now
  blended at `config.pe_stub_weight()` — default 0.0 (removed) in production; tests
  pin 0.25 for a byte-identical neural baseline. `pe_delta = -viability_pe_scale()*pc`.
- `reward_success_stub` granted a fixed pleasure pulse every 50 cycles regardless of
  behaviour. Replaced (when `config.drive_reward_enabled()`, default ON) by the
  intrinsic homeostatic-relief reward `viability.drive_reduction_reward(prev, cur,
  gain)` — phasic pleasure ∝ the per-cycle *reduction* in interoceptive drive
  pressure (Keramati & Gutkin homeostatic RL; the positive complement to the tonic
  `interoceptive_drive_pain`), bounded to [0,1] and floored into `pleasure_scalar`
  like curiosity so a real relief is felt. The legacy placeholder is retained on the
  disabled/legacy path so the test baseline is unchanged.

Files:
- decadic/config.py: + `pe_stub_weight()` (default 0.0), `drive_reward_enabled()`
  (default True), `drive_reward_gain()` (default 1.0); DEFAULT_DRIVE_REWARD_* consts.
- decadic/state/viability.py: + pure bounded `drive_reduction_reward()`; `*_stub`
  docstrings marked non-neural (numpy Phase-1 path).
- decadic/state/state_bus.py: + `prev_drive_pressure` field + snapshot key (so the
  relief delta is per-cycle and continuous across restarts).
- decadic/cycle/neural_pipeline.py: `pe_delta` uses `pe_stub_weight()`; reward block
  computes the drive-reduction relief from `prev_drive_pressure` vs the current drive
  pressure (no-op when drive off / homeostasis None), keeps the legacy stub when
  disabled; diagnostics add real keys `prediction_error_delta` / `drive_reward_delta`
  with `stub_*` back-compat aliases.
- decadic/agents/runtime.py: restore `prev_drive_pressure` in apply_checkpoint_payload;
